{:edb/db-before-t 1097 :edb/db-after-t 1098 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534410 50 #inst "2026-10-07T01:08:20.297Z" 13194139534410 true] [17592186147560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286838 13194139534410 true] [17592186147561 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286845 13194139534410 true] [17592186147561 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286852 13194139534410 true] [17592186147565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286824 13194139534410 true] [17592186147565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286831 13194139534410 true] [17592186286824 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286825 13194139534410 true] [17592186286824 1089 "q-61705" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286824 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534410 true] [17592186286824 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/4b0c67b6a8c18b4f05198c209dae8cb960c9bfdcfc8310d0f59ee7a717e68f41.png)\n\nAssuming that all side faces have the same height of $8\\,\\text{cm}$, find the total surface area of the square pyramid above using its net." 13194139534410 true] [17592186286824 1113 #uuid "2a7cfcf9-d573-54e4-af00-b3e2f3d9834c" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286824 1145 "The net of our pyramid is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/1fc39646f2b26116f97bc5340b0a7211911ba64ae59e4ce652bf13018fb7ef33.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with a side equal to $6\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=6\\times 6=36\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $6\\,\\text{cm}$ and the height is $8\\,\\text{cm}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 6\\times 8=24\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =(\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =36+4\\times 24 \\\\  & =36+96 \\\\  & =132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286826 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286827 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286828 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286829 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286830 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1041 "selection" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286826 13194139534410 true] [17592186286825 1110 #uuid "a431bdc3-b162-55af-82be-915961c75955" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286826 1034 "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286826 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534410 true] [17592186286826 1111 #uuid "534c30cd-fb91-5d73-a130-bbcbb6b18e26" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286827 1034 "116\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286827 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534410 true] [17592186286827 1111 #uuid "1a4b29d0-df4c-5668-bfcf-e3143e442641" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286828 1034 "126\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286828 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534410 true] [17592186286828 1111 #uuid "80a20c95-701b-5f59-894b-467ccfcb4639" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286829 1034 "142\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286829 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534410 true] [17592186286829 1111 #uuid "d2911c93-110c-5b4a-bbd6-1bf9a421d5a7" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286830 1034 "96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286830 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534410 true] [17592186286830 1111 #uuid "f1828f98-4786-5226-a063-0b73d2757f28" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286831 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286832 13194139534410 true] [17592186286831 1089 "q-61907" 13194139534410 true] [17592186286831 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534410 true] [17592186286831 1100 "![](/